= Tarski's definition of truth =
====== short ======
Fit for purpose - which was simply to define _*logical truth*_.

====== related to ======
[[attitudes_towards_logical_truth]]

--[[influential_semantic_theories]]
--[[moschovakis2017-senseDenotationAlgorithmValue]]

= main =
Tarski's definitions only define truth given the extension of each predicate and
reflect only the logical structure by which those predicates are combined.  For
Tarski's purpose, which was explicitly to define a notion of logical truth, this
was adequate.  

No account is offered as to how the extensions of those fundamental predicates
are fixed. (Let them be fixed how you will, it doesn't matter for the purpose of
defining _logical truth_.)

Can easily (mis)lead into feeling that the problem is to determine those
predicates extensions and that hence the approach to semantics should be bottom
up. 
